<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  org.nextbsd.powerd.plist

  Boot-time launchd plist for pmconfigd, Apple's power management daemon
  (PowerManagement-1846.120.8.0.1, src/PowerManagement). macOS ships it as
  com.apple.powerd; see PowerManagement/pmconfigd/com.apple.powerd.plist.

  THE LABEL IS NEXTBSD'S, THE SERVICES ARE APPLE'S

  The job is ours, so its label is org.nextbsd.powerd. The two MachServices
  keep Apple's names because Apple's IOKit client code looks them up by name:
  IOPMLib's MIG calls go to com.apple.PowerManagement.control
  (kIOPMServerBootstrapName) and its asynchronous assertion and user-activity
  calls to com.apple.iokit.powerdxpc. Renaming them would mean patching every
  client. Apple's third service, com.apple.powerd.lowpowermode, belongs to
  Low Power Mode, which NextBSD does not build.

  DIFFERENCES FROM APPLE'S PLIST

  - ProgramArguments is /usr/sbin/pmconfigd. /System/Library holds data
    only, never executables. pmconfigd also owns the CPU power policy, so
    FreeBSD's CPU-frequency daemon, /usr/sbin/powerd, is not shipped.
  - RunAtLoad: Apple's job starts on demand at the first lookup of either
    service. pmconfigd also has to act without being asked (power sources,
    idle sleep, lid and button policy), so it starts at boot, as notifyd
    and the other system daemons here do.
  - No JetsamProperties or POSIXSpawnType: NextBSD has no jetsam.

  KeepAlive restarts it if it exits. stderr goes to /var/log/pmconfigd.stderr
  (pmconfigd's os_log lands there), never the console.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>org.nextbsd.powerd</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/sbin/pmconfigd</string>
    </array>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>
    <key>MachServices</key>
    <dict>
        <key>com.apple.PowerManagement.control</key>
        <true/>
        <key>com.apple.iokit.powerdxpc</key>
        <true/>
    </dict>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/var/log/pmconfigd.stderr</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/var/log/pmconfigd.stderr</string>
</dict>
</plist>
